GitHub Local HTML Preview handles the URL and HTML source of a GitHub file only after the user requests a preview. This information is processed locally solely to provide the preview. The extension developer does not collect, receive, retain, sell, or use it for advertising or profiling.

The selected HTML source is held briefly in Chrome's memory-backed session storage while the preview tab opens. It is deleted immediately after one read and is never persisted or synchronized.

When the user explicitly enables Allow active content, scripts and absolute HTTPS assets referenced by the selected HTML may be downloaded from and communicate with third-party servers selected by that HTML. This mode is disabled by default and runs inside an isolated sandbox.

Website content is used only for the extension's disclosed preview feature. It is not transferred except as necessary for user-directed active content, legal compliance, or security; it is not used for creditworthiness or lending; and no person is permitted to read it.
